-# Underground Gnome Villages (v0.3.84)
+# Underground Gnome Villages (v0.3.86)
 
-- Villages generate underground in the Overworld using a dedicated NeoForge world-generation feature. Chance: approximately one placement attempt per 144 chunks, further limited by solid-rock, depth and fluid safety checks.
-- Every settlement consists of a central ellipsoid hall, four primary connecting tunnels and a variable side tunnel connecting a second residence.
-- The hall contains a new Geomantic Node, independent of natural geodes. The node retains the v0.3.83 one-time wand attunement reward and is consumed on use.
-- Other chambers include a mushroom farm (mycelium, mushrooms, composter), a smithy (anvil, furnace, blast furnace), two residential chambers, and a workshop/storehouse.
-- Floors are dressed in polished andesite; paths use deepslate tiles. Passages have solid walls, overhead cover, periodic wooden supports and torches.
-- Each village generates 8-12 ordinary Gnomes. The existing village population manager adds `ceil(ordinary / 8)` Elders as residents register. The existing village-ID and workstation assignment system assigns the Smith and Grower. Remaining ordinary Gnomes act as Delvers.
-- Generation is limited to new chunks. Existing chunks are not retroactively modified.
-- Villages have no surface entrance in this release. Delver architectural repair and relighting beyond the initial generation still need a persistent structural blueprint; foreign player/Enderman block removal and workstation restoration remain implemented from earlier versions.
+- Villages generate in new Overworld chunks, with the existing approximately one-in-144 placement attempt and underground safety checks.
+- A single open central cylindrical shaft has an interior radius of five blocks (approximately eleven blocks across), with 17 blocks of vertical clearance from floor to roof.
+- Three floors/entrance elevations are at offsets Y+0, Y+5, and Y+10, with no solid intermediate slabs across the center.
+- A two-block-wide spiral staircase follows the inside of the shaft wall. One circuit gains five blocks of height. Landings connect the spiral with north-facing corridor entrances on all three levels.
+- Eighteen recessed Glowstone lamps illuminate the shaft: six lamps per level, five blocks apart vertically. The middle ring is staggered around the circumference. None protrude into the stairs or block the entrances.
+- A Geomantic Node hangs above the lower communal plaza at Y+3. Wand attunement still consumes the node and grants the established bonuses.
+- Each level has curved, branching three-block-wide passages with two blocks of clear headroom. Tunnels are carved as continuous sampled quadratic curves, with covered roofs and periodic torch lighting.
+- Lowest level: storehouse and workshop. Middle level: mushroom farm with a Composter and a smithy with an Anvil. Upper level: two residences with Gnome Beds and separate Elder quarters.
+- Room ceilings are three blocks above their floor. Rooms on consecutive levels are separated by five blocks.
+- Villages spawn 8–12 ordinary Gnomes. The existing village population manager establishes one Elder per eight ordinary Gnomes, rounded up. Workstation professions operate unchanged.
+- The provisional 24-block horizontal/12-block vertical village-home search still applies. This change does not yet add structural repair blueprints or retroactive regeneration in existing chunks.
